<worksheet>
  <title>Quadratic modeling</title>

  <!-- Optional introduction -->
  <objectives>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <p>
                Find the best fit quadratic model for a given set of data.
            </p>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p>
                Use the model to solve quadratic equations.
            </p>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>
  
  

  <!-- Exercises start here. -->
  <introduction>
    
    <p>
        The Reduced-Gravity Program operated by NASA provides astronauts with the unique <q>weightless</q> or 
 <q>zero-g</q> environment of space flight for tests and training. The program uses a specially
modified KC-1 35A turbojet transport that flies on a parabolic path along the data given in the table.
    </p>

    <p>
    <tabular top="major" bottom="major" left="major" right="major" row="minor" column="minor" >
<row header="yes"><cell>Time (seconds)</cell><cell>Altitude ( thousands of feet)</cell>
    </row>
<row>
    <cell>10</cell>
    <cell>26</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
        <cell>20</cell>
        <cell>31</cell>
    </row>

    <row>
        <cell>32</cell>
        <cell>32.5</cell>
    </row>

    <row>
        <cell>45</cell>
        <cell>31</cell>
    </row>

    <row>
        <cell>60</cell>
        <cell>25</cell>
    </row>
</tabular>
</p>


