  </introduction>
<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
          We want to model the flight of the airplane over time.  
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                What letter would you use to represent the inputs of this model? What are the
units? What is the meaning?
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
               What letter would you use to represent the outputs of this model? What are the
units? What is the meaning? 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.25in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                What kind of data is presented in the table above? Why? Hint: look at a scatterplot.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</exercise>
<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
            Use Desmos to find a quadratic model for the flight of the airplane over time. Write your model in functional notation.  
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use this command line in Desmos to find a quadratic model for the data in the table above in the <alert>Standard form</alert>.<md>y_1\sim ax_1^2+bx_1+c</md>. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use this command line in Desmos to find a quadratic model for the data in the table above in the <alert>Vertex form</alert>.<md>y_1\sim a(x_1-h)^2+k</md>. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Use this command line in Desmos to find a quadratic model for the data in the table above in the <alert>Intercepts form</alert>.<md>y_1\sim a(x_1-r_1)(x1-r_2)</md>. 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</exercise>

<exercise>
    <introduction>
        <p>
         Use your model to predict the time(s) when the altitude of the plane is 20 thousand feet   
        </p>
    </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.25in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                State an equation you have to solve to answer this question.
            </p>
        </statement>
        <hint>
            <p>
                Use the Vertex form you found above.
            </p>
        </hint>
    </task>
    <task workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
              Solve your equation and show your work.  
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Write a sentence to explain your solution in the context of this problem.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
</exercise>

